# SFT execution status v0.75

2026-09-10. **The metered DCP/HF kernel is now integrated with a new tiny-only
coordinator and private packager.** The full tiny CPU import-to-package chain
passes, with exactly two complete checkpoint audits and aggregate requested-byte
accounting. This completes v0.74's coordinator/package software integration task.
It does not complete native host containment, real import or Gate 5.

No real checkpoint/trainer/tokenizer payloads or datasets were opened. No GPU,
inference, training, network action, installation, instance action, GitHub push
or CI was initiated. Existing code, evidence and the saved real plan are unchanged.

## Integrated path

The new `posttraining_checkpoint_import_runner_v2.py` invokes frozen kernel v5
and new `posttraining_checkpoint_package_v2.py`. Its public real-input API still
refuses before I/O. The executable entry remains restricted to explicitly bound
tiny synthetic metadata, at most one million parameters, and the unchanged
source/output/read/write/time ceilings. Approval booleans cannot unlock it.

The pure `posttraining_checkpoint_io_contract_v1.py` binds the exact existing
plan hash, DCP manifest/read limits and HF/control limits in an independently
pinned contract. It never adds a larger live-memory allowance or raises the old
plan's backend output ceiling. A metadata-only construction check accepted the
saved real plan's shape; that was not a sufficient-budget or execution test,
and no real runtime contract was saved or authorized.

Before creating an attempt, the coordinator admits aggregate read/write
envelopes. Before invoking each component it prepays that component's cap.
Unused reservations are not refunded, including after failure. The completed
result separates successful logical content requests from unspent prepaid
capacity. Original marker, path, deadline and ledger helpers remain unchanged;
markers now have versioned names and bind the I/O contract as well as the plan.

## Exactly two checkpoint audits

The coordinator no longer performs a duplicate first checkpoint content scan.
It first audits tokenizer files, then records a strict metadata-only source
snapshot immediately before v5. The frozen DCP reader performs the first complete
manifest/file audit before deserialization. Its successful audit byte/file counts
must match the same plan and the invoked manifest-bound contract. Another source
snapshot is compared immediately after kernel return.

After private packaging, the coordinator performs the second complete checkpoint
audit and second tokenizer audit, then compares a third source snapshot. Thus
success has one kernel checkpoint audit plus one coordinator checkpoint audit,
not three. The new `posttraining_checkpoint_identity_v1.py` preserves the exact
closed directory tree, file sizes, uid/gid, link and private-mode checks without
reading payloads. Snapshots stay private in memory; they are observations, not
authenticated content-audit receipts or atomic locks. Existing DCP files must
already satisfy 0600/0700 rules; no source was chmodded.

## Short-read accounting correction

Independent review found that the old generic stream verifier counted bytes
returned by a short read, then requested the remainder. This could make an
aggregate *requested-byte* claim too small even though full-read tests passed.
The frozen verifier was preserved. New `posttraining_checkpoint_audit_v1.py`
reuses its structural/path/hash checks but debits each request before `os.read`
and terminates on any short read, EOF or exception before another content read.
No refund or remainder retry is possible. Empty files require no probe read.

The packager retains tokenizer-copy semantics, lineage, receipt, manifest and
the genuine frozen worker checksum consumer. Its v0.4 receipt contains the exact
v5 kernel evidence and I/O contract. Nested counters, authority flags, audit
arithmetic, shard scratch formula and the unchanged plan's live/output ceilings
are validated before package artifacts are created. A late completion failure
can still leave provisional files, but cannot return success or grant authority.

## Verification

**711 distinct targeted tests pass, with no failures or skips.**

- 613 stdlib tests on Python 3.11.15, 3.13.7 and 3.14.6: 1.590s, 1.597s and
  1.666s. All previous 464 stdlib regressions remain included.
- 98 genuine tiny CPU tests on Python 3.13.7: 1.658s test time / 2.997s supervised
  wall time under a 60-second parent timeout. All previous 85 native regressions
  remain included.
- 162 new tests: 23 identity, 23 strict-audit, 17 contract, 61 package,
  25 coordinator-control and 13 coordinator-native tests.
- Ruff E,F,I,B,UP / py311 / line length 100 passes on all eleven new code/test
  files. Existing Torch DCP/platform/deprecation warnings remain visible.

Native instrumentation observes the audit owners/counts and three zero-content
snapshots. Aggregate successful read requests equal intercepted targeted
`read`/`pread` request sizes; intercepted writes fit the nonrefundable private
envelope. An exactly sized aggregate read cap succeeds without a third audit.
Short first-token and final-source reads stop after one short request. Forged
audit counts, changed HF counters, source mutations, consumed attempts and late
completion failures cannot produce an authoritative success. These are tiny
fixtures, not a full-repository or real-checkpoint qualification claim.

Report: `evidence/lumi-4b-sft-import-metered-coordinator-v0.1.json`.
Structural verification:
`evidence/lumi-4b-sft-import-metered-coordinator-verification-v0.1.json`.

## Next remaining boundary

The coordinator/package integration is done for the bounded tiny path. Next is
native Linux process-guardian and filesystem/network/write containment wiring,
then actual host/runtime qualification and exact input/resource compatibility.
Mac tests do not establish Linux cgroup enforcement. These logical content
ledgers exclude dependency/module reads, physical disk measurements and native
allocator RSS; metadata pickle still requires trusted hash-bound inputs.

Only after those prerequisites and separately bound execution authorization can
the real checkpoint import proceed, followed by the remaining GPU worker/profile,
data relocation and CUDA/smoke prerequisites recorded in v0.70-v0.74. A Linux CPU
environment is sufficient for containment qualification; GPU/SFT is not started
by this stage. **Gate 5 is still incomplete; execution permission and production
eligibility remain false.** No base, dataset, rights or evaluation rule changed.

HEAD remains `ecc545fc423650bf1089311915290523c10b3172`; tracked and staged diffs
are empty. This stage adds five modules, six test files, a report, its structural
verification and this status successor. All fourteen files are local/unpublished.
